-listening-test-4-1.mp3"],"order_index":1},{"id":"en-oxford-ielts-t4-l-p2","title":"Part 2","part_number":2,"passage_text":"","audio_url":"https://ielts-listening-audio.engnovatemedia.com/3219141-oxford-ielts-practice-tests-academic-listening-test-4-2.mp3","question_groups":[{"id":"en-oxford-ielts-t4-l-g2-0","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"table_completion","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 11-14","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><p>Complete the table below.</p><p>Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS for each answer.</p><table><thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">Preparing for the interview</th></tr><tr><th>What to do</th><th>How to do it</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Step 1:</strong><p></p><p>Prepare things to take.</p></td><td>Gather all documents, e.g. copies of résumé.<p></p><p>Choose <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">11</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-oxford-ielts-t4-l-q11\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> , e.g. designs, drawings, written work.</p></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Step 2:</strong><p></p><p>Get more information.</p></td><td>Check you have pen and paper.<p></p><p>Ask firm for a <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">12</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-oxford-ielts-t4-l-q12\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> .</p><p>See profiles at Chamber of Commerce, library.</p></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Step 3:</strong><p></p><p>Focus on you and the job.</p></td><td>Contact <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">13</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-oxford-ielts-t4-l-q13\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> of this or related firms.<p></p><p>Compare yourself with what is required.</p><p>Imagine likely questions and your answers.</p><p>Decide how to make up for any <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">14</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-oxford-ielts-t4-l-q14\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> you lack.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":4},{"id":"en-oxford-ielts-t4-l-g2-1","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 15-20","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><div class=\"source-section-content-wrapper\"><p>Complete the notes below.</p><p>Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS for each answer.</p><p><strong>At the interview</strong></p><p>Arrive no more than <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">15</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-oxford-ielts-t4-l-q15\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> before the time of the interview.</p><p>After you hear the question, you can <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">16</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-oxford-ielts-t4-l-q16\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> before you reply.</p><p>You can <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">17</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-oxford-ielts-t4-l-q17\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> if you don't understand what they're asking you.</p><p>Wait for them to offer you the job before you say what <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">18</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-oxford-ielts-t4-l-q18\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> you want.</p><p>Learning from the experience will make you more <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">19</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-oxford-ielts-t4-l-q19\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> in future interviews.</p><p>Pay attention to your <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">20</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-oxford-ielts-t4-l-q20\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> - it shows you have a positive attitude.</p></div></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":6}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/oxford-ielts-practice-tests-academic-listening-test-4-2.mp3"],"order_index":2},{"id":"en-oxford-ielts-t4-l-p3","title":"Part 3","part_number":3,"passage_text":"","audio_url":"https://ielts-listening-audio.engnovatemedia.com/3219140-oxford-ielts-practice-tests-academic-listening-test-4-3.mp3","question_groups":[{"id":"en-oxford-ielts-t4-l-g3-0","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"matching_features","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 21-24","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><div class=\"source-section-content-wrapper\"><p>Complete the summary below by writing NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS in the spaces provided.</p><p>To many employers, academic success and personal development as a result of being at <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">21</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-oxford-ielts-t4-l-q21\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> can be as important as course content, so choose interesting <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">22</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-oxford-ielts-t4-l-q22\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> that you may do well in. You should, however, think more carefully about your choice if your course is <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">23</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-oxford-ielts-t4-l-q23\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> . In this case the course normally includes all the modules necessary for professional training, but if you are in any doubt check with your academic department or the <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">24</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-oxford-ielts-t4-l-q24\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> at the university.</p></div></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":4},{"id":"en-oxford-ielts-t4-l-g3-1","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"matching_features","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 25-29","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><p>Write the appropriate letters A–C against questions.</p><p>Which modules have the following features?</p></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"matching-dnd-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • developing computer skills<span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">25</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-oxford-ielts-t4-l-q25\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • exemption from part of a module<span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">26</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-oxford-ielts-t4-l-q26\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • assessment by formal examination<span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">27</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-oxford-ielts-t4-l-q27\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • developing speaking and writing skills<span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">28</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-oxford-ielts-t4-l-q28\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • learning through problem solving<span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">29</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-oxford-ielts-t4-l-q29\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div></div><div class=\"options-dnd-panel dnd-panel dnd-panel--matching\"><div class=\"dnd-panel-instruction\">Drag and drop an option to fill in each blank.</div><div class=\"dnd-cards-container\"><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"A\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">A.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">Applied Chemical Engineering</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"B\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">B.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">Fluid Mechanics</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"C\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">C.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">Chemical Engineering: Science 1</span></div></div></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":5},{"id":"en-oxford-ielts-t4-l-g3-2","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"matching_features","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 30-30","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><p>Choose the correct letter, A, B or C.</p></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"><span><strong class=\"source-question-number\">30</strong><span>Which chart shows the percentage of private study time on the Spanish 1A module?</span><span><img src=\"https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/oxford-ielts-practice-tests-academic-listening-test-4-q30.png\" alt=\"\"></span></span><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">A</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-oxford-ielts-t4-l-q30\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"A\"></span><span>Chart A: 84% private study / 16% class contact</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">B</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-oxford-ielts-t4-l-q30\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"B\"></span><span>Chart B: 64% private study / 36% class contact</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">C</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-oxford-ielts-t4-l-q30\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>Chart C: 36% private study / 64% class contact</span></div></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":1}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/oxford-ielts-practice-tests-academic-listening-test-4-3.mp3"],"order_index":3},{"id":"en-oxford-ielts-t4-l-p4","title":"Part 4","part_number":4,"passage_text":"","audio_url":"https://ielts-listening-audio.engnovatemedia.com/3219139-oxford-ielts-practice-tests-academic-listening-test-4-4.mp3","question_groups":[{"id":"en-oxford-ielts-t4-l-g4-0","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"diagram_labelling","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 31-33","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><p>Label the diagram. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER for each answer.</p><p><img src=\"https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/oxford-ielts-practice-tests-academic-listening-test-4-9-diagram-6a851ea2f3b0a.jpg\" alt=\"\"></p></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"><span><strong class=\"source-question-number\">31</strong></span><span data-luma-question=\"en-oxford-ielts-t4-l-q31\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"><span><strong class=\"source-question-number\">32</strong></span><span data-luma-question=\"en-oxford-ielts-t4-l-q32\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"><span><strong class=\"source-question-number\">33</strong></span><span data-luma-question=\"en-oxford-ielts-t4-l-q33\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":3},{"id":"en-oxford-ielts-t4-l-